<p dir="ltr" data-cds-heading=""><strong>Step 1: Upload the three text files</strong></p>
<ol dir="ltr">
<li>Open your repo on github.com â†’ <strong>Add file â†’ Upload files</strong>.</li>
<li>Choose <code dir="ltr">index-html.txt</code>, <code dir="ltr">app-js.txt</code> and <code dir="ltr">airtasker-css.txt</code> from your Downloads.</li>
<li>Tap <strong>Commit changes</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p dir="ltr" data-cds-heading=""><strong>Step 2: Delete the two old files</strong></p>
<ol dir="ltr">
<li>Tap <code dir="ltr">index.html</code> in the repo, then the <strong>â‹¯</strong> menu at the top right â†’ <strong>Delete file</strong> â†’ <strong>Commit changes</strong>.</li>
<li>Do the same for <code dir="ltr">app.js</code>. Leave <code dir="ltr">styles.css</code> alone.</li>
</ol>
<p dir="ltr" data-cds-heading=""><strong>Step 3: Rename each text file</strong></p>
<ol dir="ltr">
<li>Tap <code dir="ltr">index-html.txt</code>, then the pencil (Edit).</li>
<li>In the file name box at the top, change it to <code dir="ltr">index.html</code>.</li>
<li>Tap <strong>Commit changes</strong>.</li>
<li>Repeat for the other two:
<ul dir="ltr">
<li><code dir="ltr">app-js.txt</code> becomes <code dir="ltr">app.js</code></li>
<li><code dir="ltr">airtasker-css.txt</code> becomes <code dir="ltr">airtasker.css</code></li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p dir="ltr">The names must match exactly, including the dot and lowercase letters. When youâ€™re done, the repo should list <code dir="ltr">index.html</code>, <code dir="ltr">app.js</code>, <code dir="ltr">styles.css</code> and <code dir="ltr">airtasker.css</code>, with no <code dir="ltr">.txt</code> files left.</p>
